{"uid":"59ba0264dce06342","name":"test_commit_scan_hold_answer_command_matches_actual_release_capability","fullName":"tests.test_commit_scan_escalation_digest#test_commit_scan_hold_answer_command_matches_actual_release_capability","historyId":"64c4312312206f803cd1c1e156ff9aa8","time":{"start":1791881190197,"stop":1791881190285,"duration":88},"description":"Cure task cure-01-01-9 (PRD A.1/A.6, D.1; DoD 1/4): review found that\n    a commit-scan hold does NOT always stay unanswerable by a ruling --\n    `_pause_for_commit_secret_hit` shares the `operator_input_needed`\n    reason STRING with review's own pause, and `resume_if_ruling_answers_\n    pause` releases ANY `operator_input_needed` pause whose approach\n    already carries a `rejectionSignatures` entry, whichever pause on that\n    approach is the one currently holding. This drives the ACTUAL history\n    the review probe found broken: a real `operator_input_needed` gate\n    (review's own, task 014) parks first, an operator's ruling answers it\n    (leaving `rejectionSignatures[\"1\"]` recorded and the run running\n    again), and only THEN does a commit-scan hit park a SECOND,\n    unrelated hold on the SAME approach. The digest for that second hold\n    must advertise `rule` as a real answer (not just `unpause`), and\n    running it through the real CLI/engine route must actually release\n    the gate -- the opposite of the fresh-approach case (`test_every_\n    advertised_answer_command_releases_the_commit_scan_pause` above),\n    where no signature exists yet and `rule` is rightly not advertised at\n    all.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Cure task cure-01-01-9 (PRD A.1/A.6, D.1; DoD 1/4): review found that<br />\na commit-scan hold does NOT always stay unanswerable by a ruling --<br />\n<code>_pause_for_commit_secret_hit</code> shares the <code>operator_input_needed</code><br />\nreason STRING with review's own pause, and <code>resume_if_ruling_answers_ pause</code> releases ANY <code>operator_input_needed</code> pause whose approach<br />\nalready carries a <code>rejectionSignatures</code> entry, whichever pause on that<br />\napproach is the one currently holding. This drives the ACTUAL history<br />\nthe review probe found broken: a real <code>operator_input_needed</code> gate<br />\n(review's own, task 014) parks first, an operator's ruling answers it<br />\n(leaving <code>rejectionSignatures[&quot;1&quot;]</code> recorded and the run running<br />\nagain), and only THEN does a commit-scan hit park a SECOND,<br />\nunrelated hold on the SAME approach. The digest for that second hold<br />\nmust advertise <code>rule</code> as a real answer (not just <code>unpause</code>), and<br />\nrunning it through the real CLI/engine route must actually release<br />\nthe gate -- the opposite of the fresh-approach case (<code>test_every_ advertised_answer_command_releases_the_commit_scan_pause</code> above),<br />\nwhere no signature exists yet and <code>rule</code> is rightly not advertised at<br />\nall.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791880795037,"stop":1791880795037,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791880795038,"stop":1791880795038,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791881190168,"stop":1791881190168,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"s